A Greek Grammar for Colleges — Smyth, 1920 (@greek-source-smyth: 0, is #book, #part-of @greek-scholarly-sources) { r_1HWQDW2XAJNQAXTWS9P0QT57DG
Herbert Weir Smyth. A Greek Grammar for Colleges. American Book Company, 1920. English reference grammar of Ancient Greek.

[Digital Smyth, derived from the Perseus edition](https://neelsmith.github.io/smyth/) · [Original-edition scan in the Max Planck repository](https://pure.mpg.de/pubman/item/item_402120/component/file_402119/greek_smyth1920.pdf).

Use the relevant grammar sections to support a claim about a construction in the [Greek dossier](../research/Philological-study.lingua#r_353E4E4WH3BWFHHJNZMPKBPEXF). Record the edition and section number: later revisions and online editions can use different numbering.

[Peek's introductory textbook](Ancient-Greek-Peek.lingua#r_1D87YRHMAM7FHZH3VCDY9JTHGX) supplies a first route into the language; a research interpretation requires the ability to apply grammatical and lexical evidence to the chosen passage.

**Access:** external digital reference to the historical edition; source identity and the selected revision remain part of the citation.
